$ dark extensions enable recommended
  tests on
    adds test
  tracing on
    adds traces, ps
  workbench on
    adds workbench, clear, quit
  recommended on
[exit 0]
$ dark extensions
Turn on what you want (5 of 14 on)
Each one adds commands to `dark help`. Turning one off deletes nothing.

  [x] recommended      turns on history, tests, tracing, workbench
  [ ] account          Log in to darklang.com                          not built
  [ ]   sync           Your code and drafts on every machine, throug…  not built
  [ ] ai               Ask a model from your code, or let an agent w…  not built
  [ ] compiler         Build a function into a standalone executable   not built
  [x] history          Commit what you saved, see what changed, undo
  [ ]   branches       Try an idea on a line of its own, then merge it
  [ ] http-server      Serve your functions on a local port
  [x] tests            Tests saved beside your code, run by name
  [ ]   tests-on-save  Run the tests each save touches, in the backg…  not built
  [ ] tools            Navigate, refactor, deprecate, check types, back up
  [x] tracing          Keep a record of every run, and read it back
  [x] workbench        A full-screen home: browse, edit and run in one place
  [ ]   outliner       Notes as a folding tree, in the terminal        not built

`dark extensions show <name>` says what one adds.
`dark extensions enable <name>` turns it on; `disable` turns it off.
[exit 0]
$ dark help
Darklang: a small language that keeps your code in one store, on this machine.
Write a script, or save functions and run them by name. Everything else is an
extension you turn on when you want it.

Run code
  dark run hello.dark                  a script file
  dark eval '1 + 2'                    one expression
Keep code
  dark fn Me.Hi.greet '(name: String): String = "hi " + name'
  dark eval 'Me.Hi.greet("Ada")'       call what you saved
  dark module Me.Hi - < hi.dark        save a whole module
  dark val, type, trait, impl          save one item of another kind, like fn
  dark ls Me    dark view Me.Hi.greet    dark search "split a string"
Learn
  dark docs syntax    dark docs for-ai    dark help <command>
